{"kind":"finding","id":"F-ghost-playback-004-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/GhostPlaybackEngineTests.cs","line":6743,"method":"TryResolveUnitMemberPlaybackUT_LaunchAlignment_NeverAbsentBelowSpan","category":"T3","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/GhostPlaybackEngine.cs TryResolveUnitMemberPlaybackUT; a change that returns false for every swept currentUT -> still green, so the named pad-absence guard is not pinned","what_it_asserts":"for each currentUT swept from phaseAnchor over four cadences, IF the resolver resolved, watchUT >= spanStart - 1e-6","why_weak":"the whole assertion sits inside if (resolved); a resolver that stops resolving (the same inert-resolver failure the sibling NoUnits / BeforeSpanStart tests model as a real state) makes the loop body never run and the test green, so the sweep cannot distinguish never-absent from never-resolved","proposed_action":"count resolved steps in the loop and assert the count is above a floor (for example the majority of swept steps, or simply > 0) alongside the existing in-span bound","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
